---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="About Anusheh Chaudry: AI, healthcare, and infrastructure, plus teaching at Stanford.">
  <div class="row">
    <div class="stamp"><span class="label">About</span></div>
    <div class="body">
      <h1>Hi, I'm Anusheh Chaudry.</h1>

      <figure class="photo">
        <div class="print">
          <img
            src="/photos/cherry-blossoms.jpg"
            alt="Anusheh in a burgundy coat, smiling under pink cherry blossoms by a river"
            width="720"
            height="900"
          />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <p>
        I studied computer science at Stanford on the AI track,
        and took a year off from my master's to work full time before coming back to finish it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of my work has been where AI meets health. As an undergraduate I worked with Stanford's Salisbury Robotics Lab
        on <a href="/projects">AssistEMT</a>, an LLM assistant that guides emergency medical assessments
        alongside robots that do the physical exam.
        During an internship at Inference Analytics I worked on radiology report models
        and a patient-scheduling assistant for a hospital system.
      </p>
      <p>
        After that I moved to infrastructure. At Amazon I worked on AWS Bedrock, deploying updates to Anthropic's models
        with Anthropic engineers and working on the Kubernetes-based infrastructure that hosts them, rolling changes out
        safely across model variants and regions. Before that, as an intern on Bedrock, I automated how agents get deployed into customer accounts.
        At Artemis Software Works I built agent features for its product, Surfboard, including user memory and meeting briefings.
      </p>
      <p>
        I've also taught at Stanford since 2022: <a href="/teaching">a course I brought back and redesigned, and now CS 329Z</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="stamp"><span class="label">Elsewhere</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <ul class="plain contact">
          <li><span class="label">Email</span> <a href="mailto:anushehchaudry@gmail.com">anushehchaudry@gmail.com</a></li>
          <li><span class="label">GitHub</span> <a href="https://github.com/anushehchaudry">anushehchaudry</a></li>
          <li><span class="label">LinkedIn</span> <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/anushehchaudry">in/anushehchaudry</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .body { display: flow-root; } /* keep the floated print inside the column */
  .contact li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5.5rem auto;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.35rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
